# Operator-Level Boolean Computation with Correspondence Matrices

There are two unpacked current collections: the [compiler manuscript and study](Current_Compiler_Study/README_BUNDLE.md), and the distinct [publication-readiness audit report](Current_Compiler_Audit_Report/README_AUDIT_BUNDLE.md). For the paper, start with the [current manuscript PDF](Current_Compiler_Study/02_CONTRACT_REVISION_20260926/Operator_Level_CM_Compiler_Revised_Draft.pdf) or [LaTeX source](Current_Compiler_Study/02_CONTRACT_REVISION_20260926/Operator_Level_CM_Compiler_Revised_Draft.tex), then the [revision response](Current_Compiler_Study/02_CONTRACT_REVISION_20260926/REVIEW_RESPONSE.md).

The current study folder keeps the manuscript beside its [synthetic primary study](Current_Compiler_Study/03_STUDY_DESIGN_20260926/README.md), [natural admission and correctness work](Current_Compiler_Study/04_NATURAL_CIRCUIT_EXTENSION_20260926/README.md), [natural secondary timing](Current_Compiler_Study/05_NATURAL_TIMING_20260926/README.md), reproducibility notes and reviews. The completed synthetic primary rule failed; the bounded natural secondary timing favored direct packed evaluation on all 70 complete cases. One calibration failure is retained. Matched systems comparisons, historical P14 runtime identity, and public release preparation remain open.

